# Normalize line endings. Shell scripts MUST be LF so they run on Linux/Android.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Treat image/binary artifacts as binary (also gitignored, belt-and-suspenders)
# Detached signatures are 64 RAW BYTES, not text. Without this they match `* text=auto eol=lf` above and
# git decides by a NUL-byte heuristic -- so a signature that happens to contain no NUL is treated as TEXT,
# and one that also contains the pair 0D 0A has the 0D silently stripped on commit. The corrupted sig then
# fails verification in a way that reads as "wrong key", which has already cost a release round trip once.
# ~1-in-1000 per signature: rare enough to survive by luck for a year, which is exactly the problem.
*.sig    binary
*.img    binary
*.squashfs binary
*.erofs  binary
